  "rules": [
    "Freeze exact issue conditions and dependencies before implementing a batch; later discoveries receive explicit placement.",
    "Release only after all in-scope conditions and all mandatory regression scenarios are verified on the exact artifact.",
    "Any known critical client-safety defect blocks release regardless of its planned batch.",
    "Out-of-scope historical audit conditions remain explicitly pending in their assigned batches, not passed or silently deferred as completed.",
    "Close only issues whose entire current requirements have evidence; partial issue acceptance is reported per condition and does not close the issue.",
    "Do not mark a feature as newly implemented merely because its existing implementation was audited.",
    "No automatic termination of update installations or system service processes; fault tests use isolated owned processes.",
    "Report per-batch accepted/total conditions, fixes, test results, outstanding blockers and exact package identity; avoid a global readiness percentage inferred from evidence counts.",
    "Update acceptance gate to validate the selected batch plus mandatory regressions without permitting omitted, duplicate or unassigned requirements; keep exact SHA/artifact checks."
  ]
}
